          "distinct": true,
          "id": "af22e68382b2630aa9b82d1967093fe893bce0f6",
          "message": "fix: range-check the top limb in `to_be_bytes` for widths not divisible by 8 (#19)\n\n* fix: range-check the top limb in `to_be_bytes` for widths not divisible by 8\n\nDecomposing the top limb into bytes only bounds it to a whole number of bytes. For a width which is not a multiple of 8, an unnormalised value (e.g. from `from_limbs_unsafe` or a circuit input) could therefore be serialised as a value >= 2^BITS, e.g. `[0, 0, 2^13]` in a 252-bit type. Check that the top limb fits in BITS - 120 * (N - 1) bits in that case. The pre-defined widths are all multiples of 8, so their circuits are unchanged.\n\n* docs: update SPEC.md for the top-limb range check in to_be_bytes\n\n* docs: fix a missing conjunction in SPEC.md\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EhqKvDA1t4G18DeHLTw3X4",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-05T12:08:14+08:00",
          "tree_id": "2bf94e6133c786f57aa57a99bcff244657602ce5",
