          "message": "chore!: remove `derive_from_seed` from the public API (#28)\n\n* chore!: remove derive_from_seed from the BigInt trait\n\nderive_from_seed and __derive_from_seed are testing helpers rather than\ninteger operations. They remain available as the free functions\ninternal::derive_from_seed and internal::__derive_from_seed, which return\nlimbs. The tests use a generic helper built on them.\n\nDocuments the seed length limit and the security warning on the free\nfunction, and removes the stale trait documentation.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EhqKvDA1t4G18DeHLTw3X4\n\n* chore!: make derive_from_seed internal and document it in SPEC.md\n\nRemoves internal::derive_from_seed and internal::__derive_from_seed from\nthe public API, and the __derive_from_seed wrapper, which only called\nderive_from_seed. The tests and benchmarks use derive_from_seed directly.\n\nAdds an \"Internal functions\" section to SPEC.md describing how\nderive_from_seed derives its output, why it is fully constrained, and its\nlimitations.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EhqKvDA1t4G18DeHLTw3X4",
